  - stepName: Start
    stepEvent:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
    instruction: Now we will calibrate your eye tracking so that they will appear
      to focus on what you're looking at while in passthrough. Press "B" to continue.
    activateObjects: []
    deactivateObjects: []
  - stepName: Position Target
    stepEvent:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 2057003183}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: ExperimentController, Assembly-CSharp
          m_MethodName: PositionReticle
          m_Mode: 1
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: 
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
    instruction: Please stand/sit straight up and look forward. Use the joystick
      on the left controller to position the cube so that it appears on the center
      of your visual field. You'll know if it's centered if you do NOT see yellow
      when you 1) stare at it head-on, and 2) as you rotate your head around in a
      circle. Press "B" to continue after you've confirmed the reticle.
    activateObjects:
    - {fileID: 499440788}
    - {fileID: 469513778}
    deactivateObjects: []
  - stepName: 
    stepEvent:
      m_PersistentCalls:
